meta {
  name: Check Logged Duplicate Matches for Rule
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

get {
  url: {{CRM_URL}}/duplicaterecords?$filter=_duplicateruleid_value eq {{duplicateRuleId}}
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  $filter: _duplicateruleid_value eq {{duplicateRuleId}}
}

vars:pre-request {
  duplicateRuleId: 2b79a040-ccd5-ec11-a7b5-000d3adcba42
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  Checks Dataverse's own audit trail of matches this rule has ever caught.
  Came back empty ([]) on 20 Aug 2026 — including for the known duplicate
  case pair (fee6e902-.../187c2627-...) which structurally satisfies the
  rule's conditions (same case type, same organisation, minutes apart).
  Strong evidence duplicate detection has never intercepted anything on
  incident in this org, but NOT conclusive proof it can't — an empty log is
  also consistent with real-time duplicate detection on create/update being
  switched off entirely at the org level. That toggle needs checking
  separately (Settings > Data Management > Duplicate Detection Settings in
  the maker portal, or ask the CRM team) — see
  plans/duplicate-case-creation-on-timeout-*.md, assumption 10.
  Entity set name (duplicaterecords, not duplicaterecord) was found via
  "Resolve EntitySetName by LogicalName" after guessing wrong twice first.
}
